        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(gateway): session dashboard domain — board RPCs, ticketed widgets, dashboard tool, per-agent persistence",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nGateway domain for session dashboards (design: `docs/web/dashboard-architecture.md`): sessions get a persistent \"board\" face that agents compose. This PR delivers the whole server side — protocol schemas and validators, `board.get/update/widget.put/widget.grant/event` RPCs, `board.changed`/`board.command` events, HMAC-ticketed widget serving, the `dashboard` agent tool, tier-1 state-event session notices, and SQLite persistence in the per-agent DB. UI wiring (already landed as #110644/#110728/#110740) connects in the follow-up stitch PR.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBoards are session state owned by the agent, so storage is the per-agent DB: STRICT `board_tabs`/`board_widgets` with FK cascade and layout/grant checks. Per the new additive-surface rule in AGENTS.md, the schema version stays at 13: tables are declared canonically for fresh DBs and lazily ensured once per DB handle on existing DBs (idempotent DDL, folds into the next natural bump). Downgraded builds keep working — boards are simply absent. Widget iframes authenticate via 2-minute HMAC view tickets bound to session+name+revision+persisted view-generation (no operator token ever reaches sandboxed content); reconstruction-safe (delete/recreate with identical bytes invalidates old tickets). Session reset preserves boards; session deletion removes them. Tool-call parity: the `dashboard` tool covers everything the UI can do, including `focus_tab`/`set_chat_dock` via `board.command`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo visible surface yet (agent tool + RPCs; UI stitch follows). No config surface added. No schema version bump.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Store parity suite (in-memory vs SQLite): 10/10; persistence/ticket suite 84 passed; session-deletion lifecycle, agent-DB bootstrap/migration, v13-with-tables open and v13-without-tables lazy-create paths all covered.\n- `generate-kysely-types.mjs --verify` clean; `check-changed` green remotely (16m43s full gate); autoreview clean across rounds (review found the original operator-auth serving design unusable from sandboxed iframes — replaced with the ticket scheme).\n- Contract: matches the frozen board contract + amendments (`frameUrl`, `declaredSummary`).\n",
